1) Issues encountered during building Jenkins Pipeline ( build failed for 9 times )

Issue 1: SonarQube Plugin Not Found
Error: No plugin found for prefix 'sonar'

What happened: Ran mvn sonar:sonar but Maven didn't know what the sonar plugin was.

How we identified: Checked the console output — Maven searched all plugin groups and couldn't find it.

How we fixed: Added the SonarQube Maven plugin to pom.xml:


<plugin>
    <groupId>org.sonarsource.scanner.maven</groupId>
    <artifactId>sonar-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <version>3.9.1.2184</version>
</plugin>

Issue 2: SonarQube Server Unreachable
Error: SonarQube server [http://35.166.44.155:9000] can not be reached — connect timed out

What happened: Pipeline ran inside a Docker container on EC2 and tried to reach SonarQube via the EC2 public IP.

How we identified: Realized Docker containers can't reach their host's public IP from inside.

How we fixed: Changed Jenkinsfile to use EC2 private IP:


SONAR_URL = "http://172.31.25.181:9000"

Issue 3: Java Version Mismatch
Error: UnsupportedClassVersionError: class file version 61.0, only recognizes up to 55.0

What happened: SonarQube 10.4 needs Java 17 (version 61.0) but the Docker agent only had Java 11 (version 55.0).

How we identified: Checked the Docker agent's Java version:


docker run --rm abhishekf5/maven-abhishek-docker-agent:v1 java -version
# → Java 11
How we fixed: Built a new Docker agent with Java 17:


cat > Dockerfile << 'EOF'
FROM maven:3.9.6-eclipse-temurin-17
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y docker.io && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
EOF
docker build -t krishasuman123/maven-docker-agent:v2 .
docker push krishasuman123/maven-docker-agent:v2
Updated Jenkinsfile: image 'krishasuman123/maven-docker-agent:v2'

Issue 4: Not in a Git Directory

Error: fatal: not in a git directory

What happened: The Update Deployment File stage ran git config but the workspace had no .git directory.

How we identified: Checked the Checkout stage — it only did echo passed, never cloned the repo.

How we fixed: Updated Checkout stage to actually clone:


stage('Checkout') {
  steps {
    git branch: 'main', url: 'https://github.com/krisha-manoj/Jenkinsproj.git', credentialsId: 'github-creds'
  }
}

Issue 5: Dubious Ownership in Repository
Error: fatal: detected dubious ownership in repository at '/var/lib/jenkins/workspace/jenkinscicd'

What happened: Docker container runs as root but workspace files are owned by Jenkins user (UID 105). Git blocks operations for safety.

How we identified: Added pwd and ls -la debug commands — saw .git exists but owned by different user.

How we fixed: Added safe.directory before git operations:


git config --global --add safe.directory /var/lib/jenkins/workspace/jenkinscicd

Issue 6: Nothing to Commit (sed Failed Silently)
Error: nothing added to commit but untracked files present

What happened: sed -i "s/replaceImageTag/${BUILD_NUMBER}/g" found nothing to replace because the file already had :10 instead of replaceImageTag.

How we identified: Realized replaceImageTag was a one-time placeholder that was already replaced in a previous build.

How we fixed: Changed sed to match any existing tag:


# Before (only works once):
sed -i "s/replaceImageTag/${BUILD_NUMBER}/g" deployment.yml

# After (works every time):
sed -i "s/ultimate-cicd:.*/ultimate-cicd:${BUILD_NUMBER}/g" deployment.yml

2) How to integrate it using EKS :

ArgoCD Integration on EKS — Steps Followed
Why We Moved from Minikube to EKS
Docker images built on EC2 (x86_64) couldn't run on Mac's Minikube (ARM)
Error: exec format error — architecture mismatch
Solution: Deploy ArgoCD on EKS where everything is x86
Step 1: Created New EKS Cluster

# Created cluster "jenkinsproj" from AWS Console
aws eks update-kubeconfig --name jenkinsproj --region us-west-2
Step 2: Fixed Cluster Security Group
Error: dial tcp: i/o timeout


aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress --region us-west-2 \
  --group-id sg-0022bac0229aca77e --protocol all --cidr 172.31.0.0/16
Step 3: Added IAM User Access
Error: the server has asked for the client to provide credentials


aws eks create-access-entry --region us-west-2 --cluster-name jenkinsproj \
  --principal-arn arn:aws:iam::307946644949:user/oregonuser --type STANDARD

aws eks associate-access-policy --region us-west-2 --cluster-name jenkinsproj \
  --principal-arn arn:aws:iam::307946644949:user/oregonuser \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:eks::aws:cluster-access-policy/AmazonEKSClusterAdminPolicy \
  --access-scope type=cluster
Step 4: Created Node Group (2 nodes already running)
Verified:


kubectl get nodes
Step 5: Installed ArgoCD on EKS

kubectl create namespace argocd
kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml
kubectl get pods -n argocd
Waited until all pods showed 1/1 Running.

Step 6: Created ArgoCD Application

cat > ~/app.yml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: spring-boot-app
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/krisha-manoj/Jenkinsproj.git
    targetRevision: main
    path: java-maven-sonar-argocd-helm-k8s/spring-boot-app-manifests
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: default
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      selfHeal: true
      prune: true
EOF

kubectl apply -f ~/app.yml
Step 7: Exposed ArgoCD UI
Attempted: LoadBalancer → Failed (Classic LB TLS issues, empty response)

What worked: Port-forward from EC2:


pkill -f "port-forward"
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8443:443 --address 0.0.0.0 &
Opened port 8443 on EC2 security group:


aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress --region us-west-2 \
  --group-id <EC2-SG-ID> --protocol tcp --port 8443 --cidr <MY_IP>/32
Step 8: Accessed ArgoCD UI
URL: https://35.166.44.155:8443
Username: admin
Password:

kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d; echo
Step 9: Verified Application Deployed

kubectl get applications -n argocd
# → spring-boot-app   Synced   Healthy

kubectl get pods -n default
# → spring-boot-app pods Running

